  CROSS-ROI CORRELATION, two estimators and a draw-level bootstrap.
  `all-finite` drops any ROI with a single NaN and so selects ROIs;
  `pairwise` keeps every ROI and uses joint-finite draws per pair.
  The interval is a 1000-sample bootstrap over DRAWS (pairs share
  ROIs, so an across-pair standard error would overstate precision).
