==============================================================================
  WHAT IS THE COMMON MODE?  Removing the per-draw mean across ROIs.
  If the coupling is a single per-draw global scalar -- one noise
  realisation that is simply louder on some draws than others --
  then subtracting mean_j d[j,r] from every d[i,r] must restore
  alpha to ~0.5 and rbar to ~ -1/(m-1).  If a spatially structured
  component survives, alpha stays depressed and that structure is
  the real obstacle.
